WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.616
<v Examiner>Exam case 13.

2
00:00:02.616 --> 00:00:03.543
<v Examiner>Fertility.

3
00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:06.519
<v Examiner>Rose and Simon are seeing the nurse at their GP clinic,

4
00:00:06.519 --> 00:00:08.907
<v Examiner>because they've decided to start trying to conceive.

5
00:00:08.907 --> 00:00:12.765
<v Examiner>Rose has been on the Depo Provera injection as contraception for the past two years.

6
00:00:12.765 --> 00:00:16.852
<v Examiner>As her nurse, you advise that it could take a little while for her normal cycle to settle

7
00:00:16.852 --> 00:00:18.918
<v Examiner>after coming off this hormonal contraceptive.

8
00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.847
<v Examiner>Rose takes your advice to track her cycle,

9
00:00:20.847 --> 00:00:24.108
<v Examiner>after learning there are only a few days each month when she's fertile.

10
00:00:24.108 --> 00:00:27.460
<v Examiner>She has also bought an ovulation predictor kit, and some pregnancy tests.

11
00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:32.661
Her Anatomy Mondays page names her fertility quiz as this case's model answer,

12
00:00:32.661 --> 00:00:34.793
so these answers are her quiz keys.

13
00:00:34.793 --> 00:00:38.448
And in her session, she said the cycle graph is in the exam,

14
00:00:38.448 --> 00:00:40.641
though the labels may be taken away.

15
00:00:40.641 --> 00:00:42.591
So know each curve by its shape.

16
00:00:42.591 --> 00:00:44.479
LH peaks just before ovulation.

17
00:00:44.479 --> 00:00:47.586
Progesterone is low, then peaks in the second half.

18
00:00:47.586 --> 00:00:51.119
And FSH goes with the follicular and proliferative phases.

19
00:00:51.119 --> 00:00:53.190
Her phrase: keep the F's together.

20
00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:54.185
<v Examiner>One mark.

21
00:00:54.185 --> 00:00:56.305
<v Examiner>What is an ovulation predictor kit?

22
00:00:56.305 --> 00:00:57.395
<v Examiner>What does it show?

23
00:00:57.845 --> 00:01:00.636
It shows when ovulation is about to happen,

24
00:01:00.636 --> 00:01:05.569
because it picks up the sharp peak in luteinising hormone, LH, in the urine,

25
00:01:05.569 --> 00:01:06.997
just before ovulation.

26
00:01:07.447 --> 00:01:08.115
<v Examiner>Four marks.

27
00:01:08.115 --> 00:01:09.879
<v Examiner>What occurs during ovulation?

28
00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:15.534
The hook: an LH peak, the follicle bursts, and the oocyte goes out toward the fimbriae.

29
00:01:15.984 --> 00:01:18.942
A secondary oocyte is released from the ovary.

30
00:01:18.942 --> 00:01:21.449
Ovulation is triggered by a peak in LH.

31
00:01:21.449 --> 00:01:27.172
The ovarian wall ruptures when the fluid-filled Graafian follicle, the tertiary follicle,

32
00:01:27.172 --> 00:01:27.622
bursts.

33
00:01:27.622 --> 00:01:31.609
And the force of the fluid pushes the oocyte out of the ovary,

34
00:01:31.609 --> 00:01:34.309
toward the fimbriae of the fallopian tube.

35
00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:36.317
<v Examiner>One mark.

36
00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:40.218
<v Examiner>Using the image, on what days of her cycle is a female fertile?

37
00:01:40.668 --> 00:01:42.204
Days ten to seventeen.

38
00:01:42.654 --> 00:01:43.245
<v Examiner>Two marks.

39
00:01:43.245 --> 00:01:48.265
<v Examiner>Can you explain why the hormone levels change over the course of the menstrual cycle?

40
00:01:48.715 --> 00:01:52.360
Because each hormone is driving a different process.

41
00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.743
FSH, for the follicles to develop.

42
00:01:54.743 --> 00:01:57.897
Oestrogen, for the uterine lining to thicken.

43
00:01:57.897 --> 00:01:59.159
LH, for ovulation.

44
00:01:59.159 --> 00:02:04.416
And progesterone, for the uterus to prepare for implantation and pregnancy.

45
00:02:04.866 --> 00:02:05.441
<v Examiner>Two marks.

46
00:02:05.441 --> 00:02:08.429
<v Examiner>How would pregnancy change the hormone levels graph?

47
00:02:08.879 --> 00:02:12.605
The hormone drop at roughly day twenty-one wouldn't happen,

48
00:02:12.605 --> 00:02:15.321
with successful implantation and pregnancy.

49
00:02:15.321 --> 00:02:18.479
The oestrogen and progesterone levels keep rising.

50
00:02:18.929 --> 00:02:19.538
<v Examiner>Once more.

51
00:02:19.538 --> 00:02:21.062
<v Examiner>Ovulation, and the graph.

52
00:02:23.512 --> 00:02:29.196
The ovulation predictor kit catches the peak in LH in the urine, just before ovulation.

53
00:02:29.196 --> 00:02:34.814
At ovulation, an LH peak makes the Graafian follicle burst, the ovarian wall ruptures,

54
00:02:34.814 --> 00:02:39.975
and a secondary oocyte is pushed out toward the fimbriae of the fallopian tube.

55
00:02:39.975 --> 00:02:42.262
The fertile days: ten to seventeen.

56
00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:46.247
Each hormone drives its own process: FSH grows the follicles,

57
00:02:46.247 --> 00:02:49.710
oestrogen thickens the lining, LH triggers ovulation,

58
00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:52.519
and progesterone prepares for implantation.

59
00:02:52.519 --> 00:02:56.569
In pregnancy, the drop at about day twenty-one doesn't happen:

60
00:02:56.569 --> 00:02:59.117
oestrogen and progesterone keep rising.
